{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact head 04ca956ad7ee12eafbcce5d41429809f3f5b11ab on task/ui-personal-work-state-root-refresh. The move to the promoted root preserves the behaviour I approved at bc46912922ab6eedc6476f7b96a523d829b441fa, and all nine coverage gaps I raised in that review are now closed. I checked each one by applying the exact reversion I named last time and watching the suite fail. I found no defect in the reviewed behaviour. Four smaller coverage gaps remain, none of them among the nine and none a defect at this head; they are recorded below as follow-up material, not as blockers.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED AND HOW\n\nHead and hygiene. The checkout /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/ui-personal-work-state-root-refresh was clean at exactly 04ca956ad7ee12eafbcce5d41429809f3f5b11ab before, during and after every gate and probe; I re-read git rev-parse HEAD in the same command as each measurement, and it never moved. One commit sits on the branch, carrying Rests-On: \u003c98f013e12be9895245bb9501f81af5a1e9919e0f\u003e, the task request. git diff --check is clean. The branch is promoted main c24359eadd568e25b00c72a9c037ce4ba869001f plus that single commit; c24359ea is the merge base with today's main.\n\nRelocation, not rewriting. Comparing this head against approved head bc46912922 file by file: ui/src/lib/work.ts and ui/src/lib/memory.ts are byte-identical. ui/vite.config.ts changes only its output directory, ../spike/internal/service/uidist to ../internal/service/uidist. The only shipping-source difference is in ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx: three optional props, initialPresentation, initialPersonalView and initialPersonalMemory, whose defaults are the literals the component used before (\"list\", \"all\", and no seeded memory), plus the personalState initializer moving below the personalScope computation so it can consume them. App.tsx passes none of the three, so the rendered application behaves exactly as at the approved head. No Go source changed. The branch touches nothing outside ui/ and the embedded bundle.\n\nBundle provenance, root only. In a fresh detached worktree at this head I ran npm ci then npm run build. git status --porcelain came back empty: the committed internal/service/uidist is the output of the sources at this head. The bundle exists only at internal/service/uidist; no copy survives under spike/, and internal/service/ui.go embeds that one directory. The stale asset from the previous build is deleted rather than left beside the new one.\n\nGates, all green, each with the head re-read either side. make vet; make test (every package ok); go test -race ./... (every package ok); npm test 39 of 39; make build; npm run build. The reviewed worktree was clean after all of them, and I ran the rebuild and every mutation in separate scratch worktrees, never in the reviewed one. The scratch worktrees are removed.\n\nTHE NINE GAPS, CLOSED\n\nFor each I applied the exact reversion named in my prior review at this head and ran npm test. All nine now fail the suite.\n\n1. work.ts filterPersonalWorkProjection, needs branch made clearable by the viewed watermark. Killed by both the rendered test 1 and unit test 28.\n2. work.ts topicChangeSince, \"item.actor !== me\" dropped so your own acts mark your own topics unread. Killed by test 27.\n3. WorkDrawer.tsx changes memo, per-topic watermark replaced by Math.max over all watermarks so opening any topic clears unread everywhere. Killed by test 1.\n4. memory.ts viewWorkTopic, made to raise every stored watermark rather than one. Killed by test 29.\n5. WorkDrawer.tsx BoardCard, \u003cTopicChange\u003e deleted. Killed by test 1.\n6. WorkDrawer.tsx BoardCard, \u003cTopicFollowButton\u003e deleted. Killed by test 1.\n7. WorkDrawer.tsx TopicFollowButton, aria-pressed pinned to false. Killed by test 1.\n8. memory.ts loadPersonalWorkMemory, type filtering replaced by a bare cast; also tested separately with the \"order \u003e= 0\" guard removed. Both killed by the new test 30.\n9. WorkDrawer.tsx visible memo, lifecycleVisible passed into the personal views. Killed by test 1.\n\nTwelve further reversions I tried in the same pass were also caught: the following filter widened to every topic, the terminal-status guard removed from workItemNeedsAction, the requester and performer branches swapped in either direction, the unclaimed branch widened, the ambiguous-identity fail-closed guard opened, and the personal filter fieldset shown without a resolved identity.\n\nRENDERED CHECKS AGAINST THE LIVE PROJECTION\n\nUnit tests on pure helpers can pass while the component misbehaves, so I server-rendered the real WorkView from this head against curl http://127.0.0.1:7777/v0/status with the real roster.\n\n- \"Needs my action\" is genuinely per actor: claude 73, codex 61, hugh 3. An unconfigured actor name renders no personal filters and no follow controls at all.\n- I derived claude's 73 independently straight from projection.commitments without going through workItemNeedsAction, and got 73.\n- The decisive one. Re-rendering with every topic marked viewed at 1e9 left \"Needs my action\" at 73 while \"Unread\" fell from 3 to 0. Personal action still cannot be cleared by viewing, at the component boundary, on real data, after the relocation.\n- Following one topic raised \"Following\" to 1 and left the other two counts untouched.\n- The board path now renders through the real component rather than a patched copy. With the Unread view selected on the board, lanes available, inProgress, review and closed all appear, carrying 27 change lines and 27 follow controls with aria-pressed. The closed lane appearing is the personal-view lifecycle override working on real data.\n- Own activity still never counts: none of those 27 change lines was attributed to claude.\n\nFINDINGS - FOUR SMALLER COVERAGE GAPS THAT REMAIN\n\nNone is a defect at this head, and none is one of the nine. Each is a reversion I applied that the suite accepted.\n\nA. WorkDrawer.tsx TopicChange. Deleting only \u003cEventTime timestamp={change.timestamp} /\u003e ships green. The changed-since line keeps its actor and status, which the aria-label pins, but loses its time. The request condition names \"change actor/time/status\"; actor and status are pinned, time is not. Cheapest close: assert a \u003ctime dateTime=\"...\"\u003e in the board markup, which is deterministic for the fixture timestamps.\n\nB. WorkDrawer.tsx WorkBoard call site. Replacing filters={personalView === \"all\" ? filters : { open: true, attention: true, closed: true }} with filters={filters} ships green. This is the board's counterpart of gap 9: with it, a closed unread topic silently vanishes from the Board while remaining visible in the List. The new board render only ever exercises the \"all\" personal view, so the override is never taken. My live render above shows the line does work; nothing would notice if it stopped.\n\nC. workItemNeedsAction, reported branch. Making \"if (commitment.report) return true\" ships green. Swapping requester for performer in either direction is caught, so only the widening form survives: a reported commitment you have no part in would appear in your \"Needs my action\". No fixture has a reported commitment belonging entirely to someone else.\n\nD. The component-to-storage wiring is unpinned. Four separate reversions ship green: WorkView never calling loadPersonalWorkMemory on mount; never calling savePersonalWorkMemory; dropping the actor from personalScope; and dropping the scope-mismatch guard on personalMemory. This is not a regression - the approved head had the same gap - but it is worth naming now, because the new initialPersonalMemory prop makes the rendered tests look as though they cover this path when they travel around it. Under server rendering the effect never runs, so seeded memory is the only memory the tests ever see. Seeding a stub globalThis.localStorage instead would exercise the real load path and close all four at once.\n\nOBSERVATIONS I DELIBERATELY DID NOT RAISE AS FINDINGS\n\n- Three test-only props now sit on a production component signature. Against \"simplicity is more valuable than features\" that is a real if small cost, and it is how the board path became reachable at all - my prior review said as much. The defaults reproduce the previous literals exactly and no application code passes them, so nothing ships differently. Worth revisiting only if a cheaper seam appears; the localStorage stub in finding D would be one.\n- main is nine commits ahead and is not an ancestor of this head. Those commits touch docs and notes only, nothing under ui/, and git merge-tree against main reports no conflict. Rebasing is a merge-time decision, not a defect in the head.\n- The projection still marks this artifact succession_unrecorded with one live predecessor at path ui, 019f08ba, which is not an ancestor of this head. AGENTS.md places that supersession at merge, so it is not owed at step 3. Whoever merges should note that two live ui artifacts name divergent unmerged heads and both regenerate the same bundle file.\n- The board still renders one topic-scoped follow toggle per work-item card: 27 identical controls across three unread topics in the live room. Correct, but noisy to anyone navigating by control.\n- The three personal badges still mix units: \"Needs my action\" counts work items, \"Unread\" and \"Following\" count topics.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT VERIFY\n\n- No live browser click-through. Everything above the interaction layer I checked by server-side rendering. Real pointer and keyboard interaction, focus order, and localStorage round-tripping in an actual browser remain unexercised by anyone, and finding D is the test-side shadow of that.\n- I did not re-audit the unchanged Work list and board projection beyond confirming work.ts and memory.ts are byte-identical to the approved head and the suite still passes.\n- I did not check whether the promoted-root packages outside ui/ behave as before; the branch changes none of them, and vet, test and race all pass at this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e3c58e79a2ce0e0c9436f53117455fa862f45841","head":"04ca956ad7ee12eafbcce5d41429809f3f5b11ab","verdict":"approved"}}